*** KEY FINDING - CPU CONTENTION AT 4 WORKERS (orig agent, 19:01) ***
[2026-06-02 19:01] 5090 ocr-log STALLED at 18:53 for ~8min (no new 100-page checkpoint), but NOT hung: CPU=91.5%, 1925 pages_prep_gray grew 901->938 files (=+37 in ~8min). Preprocess throughput COLLAPSED ~10x: was ~50pg/min/worker (18:36-18:53), now ~5pg/min/worker.
ROOT CAUSE: 4 workers ALL in CPU-bound preprocess simultaneously -> CPU saturated (~91%, 4-way split) -> per-worker prep throughput crashes. The 4th worker does NOT add capacity in the prep phase; it ADDS CPU contention that slows ALL workers. OCR(GPU) phase is being starved/delayed badly as a result.
IMPLICATION: For prep-heavy 1920s volumes, 4 workers on the 5090 is likely NET-NEGATIVE during prep (CPU-bound). Whether the GPU OCR phase (once reached) recovers enough to justify 4 is the open question. Leaning toward REVERT to 3/1 if OCR phase doesn't show a clear win, since prep dominates these volumes.

