================= FINAL REPORT =================
FINAL CONFIG LEFT RUNNING: 3/1 (5090 max_workers=3 via Scheduled Task PatoLex_OCR_5090, supervisor 75s stagger; 5080 = 1 worker 5080-1 via PatoLex_OCR_5080). BOTH VERIFIED PRODUCING OCR (pages advancing on both at 19:06).

4/2 pg/min: NOT MEASURABLE. 5090 at 4 workers never reached sustained GPU OCR in 23+ min - all 4 stuck in CPU-bound STAGE1-RENDER/STAGE2-PREPROCESS, GPU util 0-3% the entire time, ZERO OCR pages produced. No valid throughput window existed (page-count delta 18:41-19:01 ~= 0 net OCR on both boxes, prep-bound).

ROOT CAUSE (durable finding): OCR pipeline has a heavy CPU-bound prep stage (render@300DPI + grayscale preprocess + classify) BEFORE the GPU OCR stage. When N workers all land on fresh volumes at once they preprocess in LOCKSTEP and saturate CPU. At 4 workers the 5090 CPU hit ~91-94% and per-worker prep throughput COLLAPSED ~10x (50->5 pg/min/worker), indefinitely starving the GPU. The 4th worker is NET-NEGATIVE on prep-heavy volumes (1920s multi-vol chapter PDFs, 1500-3270 pg each). 3 workers leaves enough CPU headroom that a worker reaches the GPU stage promptly.

TELEMETRY (4/2 window, prep-phase only, n=24 samples 18:41-18:55, both boxes):
- 5090: GPU temp peak 41C / med 40C; util peak 3% / med 0%; power peak 13.9W / med 13.6W; mem peak/med 1320MiB; CPU% peak 94.4 / med 88.7
- 5080: GPU temp peak 34C / med 33C; util peak 0% / med 0%; power peak 23.4W / med 10.1W; mem peak/med 1006MiB; CPU% peak 76.1 / med 68.7
  (GPUs idle entire window -> prep-phase numbers, NOT OCR-load numbers. No >80C, no OOM, no instability ever.)

OOM/HANG: None. No OOM either box (5080 OCR model only ~1-5GB VRAM, 16GB ample). No true hang - prep kept advancing, just pathologically slow under contention. All worker bumps/kills/restarts clean (taskkill /F /T).

RECOMMENDATION: Stay at 3/1. To measure a real 4/2 OCR rate you'd need to defeat prep lockstep (pre-render volumes, or separate CPU prep pool feeding a GPU OCR pool) or test on a box with more CPU cores. As-is, the 4th worker on the 5090 hurts.
